{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head edb77c05136a75ac90f93f2cbd67cd0cedfb4664, tree 42ee49c2bb556c4e4ee103dd2a7f4db14660fe3c, on builder/dd1-descriptor-20261116, all 26 artifacts, for request c7b0d71e under my promise 05ebeca3. This verdict names the one implementation: DD-1 (request 5d48d6da, promise fc06de82, report 13e5a36e, the C4 note's DD-1 section, primary). `gs review --prepare` resolved that binding at this head, with the request closing on the sealed receipt.\n\nThe head sits on 0916bf3d, the approved EK-1/ES-1 head, not on main 9d69f807. The two trees are equal (cb5049b2), and `git merge-tree --write-tree 9d69f807 edb77c05` gives this head's tree, 42ee49c2. So a merge onto 9d69f807 lands exactly the reviewed tree. A commit-message check over 9d69f807..edb77c05 refuses, because 9d69f807 is not an ancestor. I ran it over 0916bf3d..edb77c05 instead.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- `actDescriptorDigest` in `packages/bytes/src/domains.ts`, under the new tag `artroom-act-descriptor-1`. It hashes the kind, the act's own declaration, and the item types, rules and capabilities that the act names directly. It collects the item types from `on`, each `also`, any field of type `item` and any Range. It includes the profile only when the act names a rule. It does not follow an item type's `refs` or `values`, as ruling bc3a5516 sets. The walk can match an unrelated member whose name is `rule` or `type`, but `named` keeps only names that the definition holds, so a false match can only add content to the digest, never drop it.\n- `authorization.ts`. The namespace holds the digest of each act by kind. A row's descriptor is compared with the digest of its own first version's kind. A step of another kind under an existing key stops with `version` before any digest is compared (ruling 423764c4, item 1). A new row of a kind that the definition lacks stops with `version`.\n- `draft-store.ts`, `scope-client.ts` and `draft-submit.ts`. `descriptorFor` finds a kind's digest. The client builds every act's digest once from its own definition, and `ClientOptions.descriptor` is gone, so no caller can pass a wrong value. Every place that compared one descriptor now compares the row's own act. `composeDraftCandidate` refines against the stored row's own kind and digest, after the caller has checked that row against the client's binding.\n- The tests. `act-descriptor.test.ts` pins five things:\n  - the signed Counter package keeps each digest across a version-only release;\n  - a change to one act changes no act that shares no content;\n  - a type that only refs name leaves the digest unchanged;\n  - the profile changes exactly the acts that name a rule;\n  - a missing kind has no digest.\n  \n  The descriptor-mismatch case in `scope-client.test.ts` now writes a historical value into retained rows.\n- The version rule. Only the `presentation` IDs of Lending (d9ad1767) and Counter (45a6c6ea) change, at the open 0.5.0. No signed release file changes.\n- The note. The DD-1 section states the bound of the walk, and it says that an outside adopter's retained authorization stops once with `descriptor-mismatch` at its next version.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. The 26 artifacts name the head, no path repeats, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only 9d69f807 edb77c05`.\n- The gate, END f0f80f43, on this exact head. `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-16-dd1-gate/gate.log` names head edb77c05 and tree 42ee49c2 with 0 changed files. Pins passed in 17.6 s. Plain 4994 with 1 skipped and Native 1169 with 2 skipped passed. The crossing counts were lost 0, stale 3 and no-owner 0, and the last line is \"gate passed\". No seal changes, and the pins stage passed.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check over 0916bf3d..edb77c05 passes: 4 checked, 0 flagged. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Each act's digest covers only what that act names, so a change to one act retires only that act's drafts and authorizations. The client derives the values from its own definition, so no caller supplies them.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The descriptor check is stricter than before. A key cannot change kind, and a row of a changed act stops with `descriptor-mismatch` before it signs again. The new tag is a separate domain, so its digests cannot collide with any other value's digest.\n\nSimplification: no required change. The head removes one client option and its test constants.\n\nA limit, stated for the record: a capability or rule that only another rule uses is not in the digest. A change there leaves the act's digest as it was. That follows from ruling bc3a5516's \"names directly\", and the profile and the named rule's own body are in the digest.\n\nThis approval authorizes no push, landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:13e5a36effd236b59ed0ffa1aa1dfbef2a8f32da","binding":"assigned","head":"edb77c05136a75ac90f93f2cbd67cd0cedfb4664","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:05ebeca315d24e465b514a25faa9c215593e36d7\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fc06de8276ee6b3f179c5ec67adc2fab3bc6dc1f\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b0dc47022c298a8cd3364bee3a335924db9d1e4f","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}